--- !u!114 &7000000000000000222
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7000000000000000219}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0.972549, g: 0.92549, b: 0.835294, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 12800000, guid: e3265ab4bf004d28a9537516768c1c75, type: 3}
    m_FontSize: 22
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 10
    m_MaxSize: 22
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: 'OBJECTIVE

    Villagers win when every Cursermancer is eliminated. Cursermancer
    wins when living Cursermancers equal or outnumber living non-Cursermancer Villagers.
    Neutral Cursermancers also count.


    1. ACTIONS

    Sides alternate turns
    with 5 hearts. Play your faction''s card: 2 hearts. Opponent or neutral card:
    5 hearts. Totem and other skills have their own costs.


    2. INFECTION

    A
    full board or Reeve begins the ritual. Cursermancer targets a card in the same
    row or column. Empty seats block infection.


    3. SACRIFICE

    Each on-board
    card of the voting faction chooses a different card. No self-votes. A sole card
    on the board is exempt. The most-voted cards are sacrificed; a tie sacrifices
    all tied cards. Skills can change the result.


    PURGE

    Each side has
    2 uses per match. Destroys infected cards in hands and on the board. Available
    during action turns only.


    RETURN TO HAND

    Returning your card or a
    neutral card refunds up to 2 hearts, never more than its placement cost. Totem
    refunds only 1 heart.


    CONTROLS

    Left-click to select or drag cards.
    Right-click to inspect. Each card''s description explains its skills and costs.
    ESC closes Rules and resumes play.'
